# Raye Opens Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade With ‘Joy’

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from Rolling Stone Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Looks like the theme for Thanksgiving 2026 is joy, joy, and more joy as Raye opened the postponed 100th annual Macy’s Thanksgiving Parade broadcast on Saturday with a performance of “Joy.”

From a Central Park tunnel, Raye was joined by her sisters Amma and Absolutely, who feature on the This Music May Contain Hope track “Joy,” and were Raye’s supporting acts for her This Tour May Contain New Music tour. (It’s unclear whether the performance was live Saturday or prerecorded due to scheduling conflicts from the parade’s postponement.)

Raye opens the 100th Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade with a performance of “Joy.” pic.twitter.com/v2MUPAOgOB

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

The South London singer earned a whopping 11 Grammy nominations this season including Album of the Year, Songwriter of the Year, and Non-Classical, Record of the year for her album’s lead single and viral sensation “Where is my Husband!”

The film will be released on Dec. 13, with further international screenings already planned for early 2027.

Throughout the parade, which was pushed off of Thanksgiving due to bad weather , fans can also expect to see artists including Megan Moroney, Natasha Bedingfield, Jimmy Fallon & the Roots, JoJo, Indigo Girls, and Queen Latifah.

